<article class="env-remark" id="4F3E3D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4F3E3D">Remark <span data-tag="4F3E3D">8.2.9.10</span>.</a> Let $X: \calJ \rightarrow \calC $ be as in Notation <a href="/tag/0B4785" data-tag="0B4785">8.2.9.7</a>. Then the $J$th matching object $M_{J}(X)$ can also be identified with the colimit </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varinjlim _{(f: J' \rightarrow J) \in S} X(J') \]
</div>
  <p> where $S$ is any full subcategory of $\calJ _{/J}$ with the following properties: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
Every morphism $f: J' \rightarrow J$ which belongs to $\calJ ^{R}$ and is not an isomorphism also belongs to $S$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
If $f: J' \rightarrow J$ belongs to $S$, then $J \npreceq J'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
  <p> This follows from a cofinality argument, since every morphism $f: J' \rightarrow J$ in $S$ admits a canonical factorization </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  J' \stackrel{f'}{\rightarrow } J'' \stackrel{f''}{\rightarrow } J, \]
</div>
  <p> where $f'$ belongs to $\calJ ^{L}$ and $f''$ belongs to $\calJ ^{R}$. Assumption $(2)$ guarantees that the map $f''$ is not an isomorphism. </p>
  <p>Similarly, we can replace the limit $\varprojlim _{ f: J \rightarrow J'} X(J')$ defining the matching object $M_{J}(X)$ by a limit over a slightly larger category, when convenient. </p>
</article>